The right person is able to work autonomously - someone who can build a campaign strategy from a business objective, defend it with data, and hold a professional line with senior stakeholders, including pushing back when the strategy, timeline, or resourcing calls for it.

&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities

&nbsp;

Campaign Strategy &amp; Execution

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Own ONC Pharma campaign strategy end to end - from translating business and brand objectives into an integrated, multi-channel campaign plan through launch, in-flight optimization, and retrospective.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Direct day-to-day execution across channels (digital, email, paid media, content, HCP/patient-facing programs, events), making prioritization calls and tradeoffs as they arise.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Set the campaign brief and creative direction in partnership with creative and brand teams, ensuring every asset ladders back to strategy.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Proactively surface risks to timeline, budget, or performance and drive them to resolution - rather than escalating and waiting.

&nbsp;

Performance Measurement &amp; Optimization

&nbsp;

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Define the KPIs and measurement framework for each campaign; monitor performance in flight rather than only in retrospective.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Read measurement results critically - translate what happened into specific, actionable tweaks, tests, and recommendations for what to do next.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Build a continuous test-and-learn discipline into every campaign cycle, and codify what's learned so it compounds across campaigns.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Present performance results and strategic recommendations directly to senior stakeholders, including the ONC Marketing VP, with clear, well-substantiated rationale.

&nbsp;

Cross-Functional &amp; Agency Leadership

&nbsp;

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Serve as the senior point of coordination across creative, agency and media partners and marketing operations.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Drive alignment among stakeholders with competing priorities by facilitating decisions - not simply routing requests or escalating every conflict.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Manage agency and vendor relationships, holding partners accountable to strategy, quality, and timeline, and redirecting work that misses the mark.

&nbsp;

Executive Partnership - Managing Up

&nbsp;

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Partner closely with the ONC Marketing VP as a strategic thought partner, bringing a well-reasoned point of view rather than waiting for direction.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Hold the line on campaign strategy, scope, and prioritization decisions under pressure or scope creep, communicating disagreement professionally and constructively.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Know when to resolve versus escalate, and when escalating, bring options and a recommendation rather than an open question.

•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Give direct, constructive feedback up and across the organization, including to more senior stakeholders, in service of the campaign and the business.

&nbsp;

